<title>FINLAND: FINNISH 1997-98 DEFICIT, DEBT TO MEET EMU CRITERIA.</title>
<headline>FINNISH 1997-98 DEFICIT, DEBT TO MEET EMU CRITERIA.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finland's public sector deficit and debt in relation to gross domestic product (GDP) in 1997 and 1998 would be well inside the criteria for membership of EMU, the EU Commission said on Wednesday in a forecast.</p>
<p>It put Finland's public sector deficit at 1.9 percent of GDP this year and at 0.6 percent in 1998. The maximum allowed for participation in European economic and monetary union is three percent.</p>
<p>The Finnish gross public debt to GDP would be 59.2 percent this year ands 58.6 percent in 1998, the commission said. The EMU entry limit is 60 percent.  </p>
<p>Following are the economic forecasts by the European</p>
<p>Commission for Finland</p>
<p>				     1997	 1998</p>
<p> GDP growth			4.4	   3.6</p>
<p> Investment			6.0	   5.1</p>
<p> GDP price deflator	    0.9	   1.4</p>
<p> Unemployment		   14.0	  12.9</p>
<p> Public sector deficit	 1.9	   0.6</p>
<p>(pct of GDP)</p>
<p> Debt/GDP ratio		 59.2	  58.6</p>
